From 1fdc67c201f3071b008469f982b1a249502493cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nixos-m4pro <local@local>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:08:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] arm64: dts: apple: j614s: PMGR domains from this
 machine's ADT

t6040.dtsi reuses the M4 Max (t6041) PMGR list and deletes parts of it.
For J614s, use a list generated from the machine's own Apple device tree
by nixos-m4pro pmgr-dtsi instead: 195 domains, CPU domains left out as in
Asahi's files. It drops six M4 Max-only domains t6040.dtsi kept
(dispext2_cpu/fe/sys, isp_cpu, isp_fe, prores), whose registers do not
exist here. Offsets of the 195 shared domains match the M4 Max file.

t6041.dtsi now includes T604X_PMGR_DTSI (default t6041-pmgr.dtsi), and the
delete-node lists are skipped when T604X_PMGR_FROM_ADT is set.
---
 .../boot/dts/apple/t6040-j614s-pmgr.dtsi      | 1817 +++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6040-j614s.dts     |    5 +
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6040.dtsi          |    2 +
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6041.dtsi          |    6 +-
 4 files changed, 1829 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6040-j614s-pmgr.dtsi

